From f0b857a6d6f209b656553509de385d4ea7439e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:40:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/32] fix(desktop): narrow right-sidebar toggle heals the
 pane instead of no-oping
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On a phone the show-right-sidebar press dispatched PANE_TOGGLE_REVEAL with
the 'file-browser' alias, but the files pane sat outside collapsibles — its
visibility binding hides it while $fileBrowserOpen is false (the rail boots
closed), and a stale dismissal removes it from the tree — so the handler's
match lookup returned and the press did nothing (r6's zero-code M3 verdict
only held after desktop-width preprocessing). When the id resolves to a
registered collapsible pane that isn't currently revealable, run it through
revealTreePane (un-dismiss, adopt, un-hide, un-collapse its column) and
open the drawer anyway; unknown ids still no-op. The backdrop gains a
data-narrow-backdrop marker for the same reason the drawer and close button
have theirs. Regression tests cover the hidden-pane and dismissed-pane
routes with backdrop + close-button assertions.
